    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d442">

                <pb facs="0462" n="442" xml:id="pg442"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Burlingame</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 77.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-09-20"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 20, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    despatch of the 3d of June, No. 80, suggesting an instruction from this
                    department to consular officers in China, to the effect that in all cases of
                    conflict growing out of the alleged improper conduct of an officer subordinate
                    to a consul, the consul general shall have power to suspend such officer,
                    pending a reference to the minister at Peking, who, if he shall approve the act
                    of the consuls general, shall remove such officers, subject to the approval of
                    this government. In reply, I have to inform you that such an instruction will be
                    issued without delay.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Anson Burlingame</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
